{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-j3q9-mxjg-w52f","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j3q9-mxjg-w52f","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/pillarjs/path-to-regexp/security/advisories/GHSA-j3q9-mxjg-w52f","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4926","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"],"description":"path-to-regexp vulnerable to Denial of Service via sequential optional groups","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","epss":0.0004,"percentile":0.12139,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","cwe":"CWE-1333","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["8.4.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"8.4.0","date":"2026-03-28","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.030000000000000002},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-4926","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4926","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"],"description":"Impact:\n\nA bad regular expression is generated any time you have multiple sequential optional groups (curly brace syntax), such as `{a}{b}{c}:z`. The generated regex grows exponentially with the number of groups, causing denial of service.\n\nPatches:\n\nFixed in version 8.4.0.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nLimit the number of sequential optional groups in route patterns. Avoid passing user-controlled input as route patterns.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","epss":0.0004,"percentile":0.12139,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","cwe":"CWE-400","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-4926","cwe":"CWE-1333","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"path-to-regexp","version":"8.3.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-j3q9-mxjg-w52f","versionConstraint":">=8.0.0,<8.4.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"8.4.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/path-to-regexp@8.3.0?package-id=c9161432c802a485","name":"path-to-regexp","version":"8.3.0","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/hbase-website/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:path-to-regexp:path-to-regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to-regexp:path_to_regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to_regexp:path-to-regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to_regexp:path_to_regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to:path-to-regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to:path_to_regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to:path-to-regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to:path_to_regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path:path-to-regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path:path_to_regexp:8.3.0:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/path-to-regexp@8.3.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-37ch-88jc-xwx2","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-37ch-88jc-xwx2","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/pillarjs/path-to-regexp/security/advisories/GHSA-37ch-88jc-xwx2","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4867","https://blakeembrey.com/posts/2024-09-web-redos","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9wv6-86v2-598j","https://github.com/pillarjs/path-to-regexp/releases/tag/v.0.1.13"],"description":"path-to-regexp vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service via multiple route parameters","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4867","epss":0.00038,"percentile":0.11322,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4867","cwe":"CWE-1333","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["0.1.13"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"0.1.13","date":"2026-03-28","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.028499999999999998},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-4867","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4867","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://blakeembrey.com/posts/2024-09-web-redos","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9wv6-86v2-598j"],"description":"Impact:\n\nA bad regular expression is generated any time you have three or more parameters within a single segment, separated by something that is not a period (.). For example, /:a-:b-:c or /:a-:b-:c-:d. The backtrack protection added in path-to-regexp@0.1.12 only prevents ambiguity for two parameters. With three or more, the generated lookahead does not block single separator characters, so capture groups overlap and cause catastrophic backtracking.\n\nPatches:\n\nUpgrade to path-to-regexp@0.1.13\n\nCustom regex patterns in route definitions (e.g., /:a-:b([^-/]+)-:c([^-/]+)) are not affected because they override the default capture group.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nAll versions can be patched by providing a custom regular expression for parameters after the first in a single segment. As long as the custom regular expression does not match the text before the parameter, you will be safe. For example, change /:a-:b-:c to /:a-:b([^-/]+)-:c([^-/]+).\n\nIf paths cannot be rewritten and versions cannot be upgraded, another alternative is to limit the URL length.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4867","epss":0.00038,"percentile":0.11322,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4867","cwe":"CWE-1333","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"path-to-regexp","version":"0.1.12"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-37ch-88jc-xwx2","versionConstraint":"<0.1.13 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"0.1.13"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/path-to-regexp@0.1.12?package-id=f31955bd7f537481","name":"path-to-regexp","version":"0.1.12","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/hbase-website/package-lock.json","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:path-to-regexp:path-to-regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to-regexp:path_to_regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to_regexp:path-to-regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to_regexp:path_to_regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to:path-to-regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path-to:path_to_regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to:path-to-regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path_to:path_to_regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path:path-to-regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*","cpe:2.3:a:path:path_to_regexp:0.1.12:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/path-to-regexp@0.1.12","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-27v5-c462-wpq7","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-27v5-c462-wpq7","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/pillarjs/path-to-regexp/security/advisories/GHSA-27v5-c462-wpq7","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4923","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://makenowjust-labs.github.io/recheck/playground"],"description":"path-to-regexp vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service via multiple wildcards","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":5.9,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4923","epss":0.0004,"percentile":0.12184,"date":"2026-03-29"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-4923","cwe":"CWE-1333","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["8.4.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"8.4.0","date":"2026-03-28","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.0218},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-4923","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-4923","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html"],"description":"Impact:\n\nWhen using multiple wildcards, combined with at least one parameter, a regular expression can be generated that is vulnerable to ReDoS. This backtracking vulnerability requires the second wildcard to be somewhere other than the end of the path.\n\nUnsafe examples:\n\n/*foo-*bar-:baz\n/*a-:b-*c-:d\n/x/*a-:b/*c/y\n\nSafe examples:\n\n/*foo-:bar\n/*foo-:bar-*baz\n\nPatches:\n\nUpgrade to version 8.4.0.\n\nWorkarounds:\n\nIf you are using multiple wildcard parameters, you can check the regex output with a tool such as https://makenowjust-labs.github.io/recheck/playground/ to confirm whether a path is vulnerable.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":5.9,"exploitabilitySco